        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
          "literal": "После печати одной стороны листы снова пропускают через пресс для печати оборота, а затем дают краске закрепиться.",
          "literalSHA256": "1b8c6077cdc86828470c28ea83f2d68766f24ff0e9f515a24e3a72d19f9609d2",
          "primaryGround": "L46 states sheets go through the press again for the reverse side and are set aside while ink cures before finishing. This is distinct from the prompt/key fact of single-sheet infeed.",
          "locator": "L46",
          "sourcePaths": [
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.html",
