      "absoluteDifficulty": {
        "level": "easy",
        "status": "PASS",
        "audienceGround": "The question asks a concrete action on a visible paper stack before feeding: hoses lift sheets individually. The choices are ordinary press-workflow actions, and the keyed relation can be understood without specialist print knowledge."
      },
      "mainDistinctness": {
        "status": "PASS",
        "reason": "materials-paper-cellulose asks which material is normally used for book pages, keyed to paper. This candidate asks what vacuum hoses do to a paper stack at press infeed, keyed to lifting sheets individually. It tests a different action/relation; adding only offset context to a material-identification question would not pass."
